              "limitations": [
                "HUD FY2026 VLI limits for family sizes 1-8 in the St. Louis, MO-IL HUD Metro FMR Area are from the official Section 8 Income Limits PDF, page 52 (SHA-256 9ab4e7368299aa61f63fb3cfe566d05f64224a40910c0ed77fd5f50ecb8da3a7). A direct WSL download returned HTTP 200; Core policy reader returned HTTP 202, so machine provenance remains unverified.",
                "Above the applicable threshold is above the general very-low-income screen only, not a complete HCV ineligibility result. SLHA describes low-income families up to 80% of area median income as an eligible income category; this record does not map that pathway.",
                "The record is scoped to St. Louis City for UC-3-S2 and is not generalized to St. Louis County or other PHA jurisdictions.",
                "SLHA's HCV page reported on 2026-11-22 that its waitlist was closed and not accepting applications. This is time-sensitive application availability, not a criteria outcome; confirm directly with the PHA before action.",
                "SLHA’s income-limits page does not show an effective year and differs from HUD FY2026 for family sizes 7 and 8. The official HUD FY2026 PDF is the threshold source for this mapping.",
                "The Core source reader permits SLHA's .org domain class for discovery but reports it as unverified. The operator-reviewed local application details are context and instructions, not executable eligibility rules.",
                "Citizenship or eligible non-citizen status, household and admission conditions, local preferences, application windows, funding, and housing availability are not evaluated. Check the local PHA before action."
              ]
